{
  "area": "build",
  "description": "AGSC-06-21 with AGSC-06-16 and AGSC-06-23: a search index above 500 items. The 502 items are listed in descending slug order, so a writer that cuts shards in input order puts n-0502 in the first shard and fails. Derivation from the rule text: above 500 items the index is sharded as /search-<nn>.json, zero-padded from 01, in slug order, every shard carrying the docs of at most 500 items, so /search-01.json carries n-0001 to n-0500 and /search-02.json carries n-0501 and n-0502; /search.json is then the manifest {shards, docs_total}, whose bytes are JCS plus one LF (AGSC-04-04): docs_total 502 and the two shard paths in order. Each shard is a complete AGSC-06-16 index over its own slice whose postings count from zero in its own docs[]: the title Note 0501 tokenizes to note and 0501 (AGSC-06-23), so the second shard's whole bytes carry note with the postings [0,1] — not [500,501], the other reading, which answers wrongly on every shard but the first. The first shard is asserted by its number of docs and its first and last slug.",
